# Trivy ignore list — reviewed, non-applicable advisories only.
# An advisory accepted in osv-scanner.toml is mirrored here, and in
# pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas (package.json), only where Trivy or pnpm audit
# would otherwise report it. Keep the rationale in sync wherever an entry
# appears. The lists differ on purpose, as of 2026-11-02:
#   - deepmerge GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4 is in osv-scanner.toml only. GitHub rates
#     it Low, below this scan's CRITICAL/HIGH and below both levels the repo
#     runs pnpm audit at (high in security.yml, moderate in guard:audit-clean).
#   - minimatch GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 is in osv-scanner.toml and pnpm.auditConfig
#     only. GitHub rates it Moderate, below this scan's CRITICAL/HIGH;
#     guard:audit-clean (moderate) reports it, so pnpm.auditConfig needs the
#     mirror.
#   - brace-expansion GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg is here and in pnpm.auditConfig, but
#     osv-scanner.toml dropped it once the overrides cleared it. Neither Trivy
#     nor pnpm audit reports it without these entries (checked 2026-10-30), so
#     both are dead and left for their own removal. Until then they would hide
#     a regression below the override pins from Trivy and pnpm audit (only the
#     OSV gates would catch it), and the comment below names versions the
#     lockfile no longer has.
# Every entry below is against pnpm-lock.yaml. This file is also the only one
# of the three that covers apps/blackout-server/poetry.lock (the OSV gates and
# pnpm audit read pnpm-lock.yaml alone); the four Twisted 26.4.0 entries it
# held for that lock left on 2026-11-02, when Twisted 26.10.0 was locked.
# Records: docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-30.md,
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-31.md and
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-twisted-2026-11-02.md.

# brace-expansion ReDoS. The tree resolves to 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.8, all at or
# above the maintainer's per-line security patches (1.1.12/2.0.2/5.0.8); OSV's
# affected-versions list for the 1.x line tops out at 1.1.11, so 1.1.16 is
# patched. The scanners over-report across major lines. CVE-2026-14257 is the
# CVE alias of GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (Trivy matches by CVE); both are listed.
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg
CVE-2026-14257

# image-size 1.2.1 (pnpm-lock.yaml): infinite-loop DoS, two advisories of one
# class: crafted JXL/HEIF box types (GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq, 1.2.0 and later) and
# a zero-length ICNS entry (GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr, 0.6.3 and later). Both are
# fixed in 2.0.3 (npm, 2026-09-14), which OSV and GitHub list as the fix; the
# 1.x line has no fixed release (1.2.1 is its newest, npm's `legacy` tag).
# Not taken: the one consumer, metro 0.83.5 (React Native's bundler, reached
# through react-native 0.82.1 -> @react-native/community-cli-plugin 0.82.1 in
# packages/ui and legacy/blackout-web), requires image-size ^1.0.2, and its
# getAssetData passes a file path to imageSize(), which 2.x no longer accepts
# (imageSize() takes a Uint8Array only; file reads moved to the async
# image-size/fromFile), so an override to 2.x would break metro's asset
# pipeline. metro 0.83.8 (the 0.83-stable tag, 2026-08-19) dropped image-size
# for its own parser and is inside the plugin's ^0.83.1, so a metro update
# within range removes the package and these entries; that is a React Native
# toolchain refresh of its own, not done here and due before 2026-11-30.
# Build-time only: no metro config, script or workflow in this repository runs
# metro. If something did, metro would parse only image files on disk at
# bundle time: files in this repository (packages/ui and legacy/blackout-web
# track no image file) and files of installed packages, such as
# react-native's LogBox PNGs; never remote or user-supplied input. Mirrored in
# osv-scanner.toml (ignoreUntil 2026-11-30) and pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas
# (no expiry there). Here each line carries exp:2026-11-30, which Trivy
# honours. Until 2026-11-02 this comment said no fixed version existed; that
# had been false since 2026-09-14. CVE aliases listed alongside the GHSAs
# because Trivy matches by CVE. Records:
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-30.md and
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-twisted-2026-11-02.md.
GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-71329 exp:2026-11-30
GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-71330 exp:2026-11-30
